pseudo-Boolean proof version 2.0
* Regression test (wrong verdict): the same vacuous `sol` as
* incorrect/version2/order_definition_sol, one subcontext deeper.
*
* `transitivity` does not swap the database itself -- `def_order` already did
* -- but it runs inside the swapped one, and `Subcontext::Transitivity` is no
* more `is_subproof()` than `Subcontext::Order` is, so it was equally
* unguarded. It is listed separately because the fix answers the two contexts
* on separate branches: the order's structural keywords are legal here and in
* the `def_order` body, while the derivation rules of a `spec` block are legal
* in neither. The `proof` body inside this same block was never exposed --
* `OrderProofRule` pushes a `Subcontext::Subproof`, which the older gate did
* cover.
*
* Same unsatisfiable formula and same `s VERIFIED SATISFIABLE` as
* order_definition_sol.
f 2
pre_order simple
    vars
        left u1
        right v1
        aux
    end
    def
        -1 u1 1 v1 >= 0 ;
    end
    transitivity
        sol x1
        vars
            fresh_right w1
        end
        proof
            proofgoal #1
                p -2 -3 + -1 +
            end -1
        end
    end
end
output NONE
conclusion SAT
end pseudo-Boolean proof
